+#### Context on demand
+
+A llama.cpp model holds its context (the KV cache and the compute buffers) for as long as it is loaded. With `context_on_demand` the model stays loaded and a request can give the context back after its answer; the next request creates it again, which costs far less than loading the model. It suits models that are asked rarely and whose memory another model could use in between.
+
+| Option | Type | Default | Description |
+|--------|------|---------|-------------|
+| `context_on_demand` | bool | `false` | Let a request free the context after its answer, keeping the model loaded (upstream `--context-on-demand`). The load is refused with speculative decoding (a draft model, MTP) or a multimodal projector. |
+| `keep_context_ms` | int | unset | The keep, in milliseconds, given to a request that carries none (upstream `--keep-context-ms`). Unset: such a request leaves the context loaded. |
+| `context_canary` | bool | `true` | Hold each context created after the load to the output the load's context gave for a fixed input, and refuse the request of a context that does not reproduce it (upstream `--no-context-canary` switches it off). |
+
+A request says how long its context is kept after the answer with the `keep_context_ms` key of its `metadata`:
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:8080/v1/embeddings -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{
+  "model": "my-embedder",
+  "input": "hello",
+  "metadata": { "keep_context_ms": "0" }
+}'
+```
+
+- `0` frees the context as soon as the model is idle. `N` keeps it N milliseconds, so that requests following each other do not create one each. Among the requests that carry a keep the latest deadline wins: a keep never shortens another's.
+- A request without the key leaves the context loaded, as without the option, unless the model sets `keep_context_ms`.
+- Rerank requests carry no `metadata`: give the model a `keep_context_ms`.
+- A request whose context cannot be created (the memory it needs is in use) or whose context fails the canary gets an error and can be sent again.
+- Over gRPC, an `Embedding` answer carries the trailing metadata `llama-context-created-us`: the microseconds the creation took when the context was created for that call, `-1` when it was already there. One refused on the canary carries `llama-context-canary: failed` beside its error.
+
